## Test Anti-Pattern Audit — Severity-Ranked Findings

This test suite is a textbook example of **"coverage without verification"** — every production method is invoked (achieving line coverage), but almost nothing is actually asserted.

---

### 🔴 CRITICAL — Assert-Free / Assert-Trivial Tests

| # | Test | Anti-Pattern | Production Bug Risk |
|---|------|-------------|---------------------|
| 1 | `AddProduct_Works` (L19-21) | **No assertion at all.** Only proves no exception was thrown. | `Save()` could silently no-op; you'd never know. |
| 2 | `UpdatePrice_Works` (L34-35) | **No assertion.** Calls `UpdatePrice` but never checks the price changed. | Price could remain 9.99; production ships wrong prices. |
| 3 | `RemoveProduct_Works` (L39-42) | **No assertion.** Never verifies the product is actually gone. | `Delete` could be a no-op. |
| 4 | `GetProductCount_Works` (L64-66) | **No assertion.** Doesn't even add products first — meaningless exercise. | Count logic could return -1. |
| 5 | `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (L69-74) | **No assertion.** Never checks that prices actually decreased. | Discount formula `Price * (1 - fraction)` could be inverted or rounded wrong. |
| 6 | `ImportFromCsv_Works` (L85-88) | **No assertion.** Never checks products were persisted. | Parsing could silently swallow errors. |

---

### 🟠 HIGH — Weak / Meaningless Assertions

| # | Test | Anti-Pattern | Fix |
|---|------|-------------|-----|
| 7 | `GetProduct_Works` (L28) | `Assert.IsNotNull` — only checks *something* came back, not *the right thing*. | Assert on `Sku`, `Name`, and `Price` values. |
| 8 | `SearchProducts_Works` (L51) | `Assert.IsNotNull` on a `List<>` — lists are never null, so this always passes even if empty. | Assert `results.Count == 1` and `results[0].Name == "Widget"`. |
| 9 | `ExportToCsv_Works` (L81) | `Assert.IsNotNull` on a string — `string.Join` never returns null. | Assert the CSV content matches expected format. |
| 10 | `GetAllProducts_Works` (L59) | `Assert.IsNotNull` — same issue as Search; never checks count or content. | Assert `all.Count == 1` and verify the product. |

---

### 🟡 MEDIUM — Missing Negative / Edge-Case Tests

| # | Missing Scenario | Production Risk |
|---|-----------------|----------------|
| 11 | `UpdatePrice` with non-existent SKU | `KeyNotFoundException` path is never tested — contract could regress silently. |
| 12 | `GetProduct` for missing SKU | Never verifies `null` is returned for cache-miss. |
| 13 | `ImportFromCsv` with malformed input | No test for bad data — `decimal.Parse` will throw, but is that the desired behavior? |
| 14 | `ApplyBulkDiscount` with 0% or 100% | Boundary values untested. |

---

### Concrete Fixes (representative examples)

```csharp
// FIX for UpdatePrice_Works
